.nh
.TH "GUMROAD" "1" "Sep 2026" "Gumroad" "Gumroad CLI"

.SH NAME
gumroad-admin-users-refund-all-for-fraud - Queue fraud refunds for every remaining purchase of a suspended seller


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgumroad admin users refund-all-for-fraud [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Queue refunds for all successful, non-refunded purchases of a suspended seller
as fraud. The server validates and enqueues a background job; refunds are
processed asynchronously with per-purchase retries. Completion is recorded as a
comment on the seller account and in the admin audit log.

.PP
By default buyers are NOT blocked (seller-fraud case: the buyers are victims).
Pass --block-buyers only when the buyers themselves are fraudulent (self-purchase
or card-testing ring); that variant also blocks each buyer's email, card
fingerprint, browser, and IP platform-wide.

.PP
--expected-email and --expected-count are required stale-state guards: the server
responds 409 if either does not match the current account state. The seller must
already be suspended; suspend first with 'gumroad admin users suspend'.

.PP
Requires the bulk endpoint POST /internal/admin/users/refund_all_for_fraud on
the Gumroad API.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--block-buyers\fP[=false]
	Also block every buyer platform-wide (only for buyer-fraud cases like card-testing rings)

.PP
\fB--expected-count\fP=0
	Expected number of refundable purchases (required; the server rejects a mismatch)

.PP
\fB--expected-email\fP=""
	Optional current email guard

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for refund-all-for-fraud

.PP
\fB--user-id\fP=""
	User external ID (required)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Enable debug logging to stderr

.PP
\fB--dry-run\fP[=false]
	Preview mutating requests without executing them

.PP
\fB--jq\fP=""
	Filter JSON output with a jq expression

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Output as JSON

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	Disable color output

.PP
\fB--no-image\fP[=false]
	Disable image rendering

.PP
\fB--no-input\fP[=false]
	Disable interactive prompts

.PP
\fB--non-interactive\fP[=false]
	Run in explicit CI/agent mode

.PP
\fB--page-delay\fP=0s
	Wait between paginated --all requests (e.g. 200ms, 1s)

.PP
\fB--plain\fP[=false]
	Output as plain tab-separated text

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Suppress non-essential output

.PP
\fB--yes\fP[=false]
	Skip confirmation prompts


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  gumroad admin users refund-all-for-fraud --user-id 2245593582708 --expected-email seller@example.com --expected-count 18 --dry-run
  gumroad admin users refund-all-for-fraud --user-id 2245593582708 --expected-email seller@example.com --expected-count 18 --yes
  gumroad admin users refund-all-for-fraud --user-id 2245593582708 --expected-email seller@example.com --expected-count 18 --block-buyers --yes
.EE


